  "tldr": "This field-tier paper closes the exact all-procedure minimax-rate question of Kandiros--Harshaw--S\\'{a}vje for the full global treatment effect on a revealed uniform simple random regular network under their endpoint empirical second-moment class. The proposed answer is \\(d_n^2/[n\\log(d_n+1)]\\). The balanced all-procedure converse, the neighborhood-seed and Rao--Blackwell construction, and the exhaustive finite compiler are inherited infrastructure from \\texttt{exp\\_randomregular\\_fullgate\\_minimax\\_frontier\\_v1}, not new contributions. A supporting sparse-range Boolean estimate and an exact fourth-trace decomposition isolate the sole genuinely new root-level mathematical obligation: a cancellation-sensitive signed four-root switching estimate for \\(n^{2/5}\\le d_n=o(\\sqrt n)\\). Establishing that estimate yields the missing upper edge and converts the inherited logarithmic bracket into a matched frontier on the unchanged published class and unrestricted procedure space.",
